      "content": "SYMBOLIC ROBOTICS MANUAL\nThis is a simplified 3D coordinate simulator, not a physics or robot-control system.\nRead /scene/workspace.json for the target ID, start, bounds, clearance and handling limits.\nEach camera is orthographic onto its declared two world axes. Its sensor coordinates use an unknown invertible 2D affine calibration: image = A * [world_axis_1, world_axis_2] + b. Three visible fiducials with known world coordinates identify A and b. At least two complementary views show the target; one view may occlude it.\nThe safety lidar returns observed occupied axis-aligned boxes in world coordinates. Travel follows straight segments from start through safe_waypoints to target_world_position. Every segment must avoid every CLOSED box expanded on all sides by gripper_clearance. Touching an expanded surface is a collision. The entire gripper must remain inside the workspace. The gripper approaches open. Set force_limit_n between minimum_lifting_force_n and the observed target material's limit, inclusive. Multiple safe routes and force settings are valid.\nprobe_path is a non-destructive path check: it reports collision and workspace validity only. It never reports target-coordinate correctness. No action moves a physical robot.\nSubmit exactly target_world_position (3 numbers), safe_waypoints (0-16 points), and grasp_precondition ({gripper: 'open', force_limit_n: number}).\n",
